   "subject": "Shiny withProgress bar css style",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>The shiny progress bar is a nice feature, but I am wondering if we can change the style of the message box through css. Currently I have</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">progress </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  top</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">important</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  left</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">important</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  margin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">top</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">100px</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">important</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  margin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">left</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">250px</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">important</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>  color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#020202;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  font</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">18px</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  background</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#020202;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">align</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> center</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div>But it does not change the background of the message box. If someone can point me to the right place for all the customization options, that will be really great. </div></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you. </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "4pG5g3lq6AYJ",
   "from": "Winston Chang",
   "author": "55771919c42cb6a1",
